{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>רכיל בעמיך</b> — plene with yod, for the talebearer transgresses all Ten Commandments. In the Jerusalem Talmud it is permissible to speak lashon ha-ra about disputing parties, as it is stated: לא תלך רכיל [בעמיך בעושה מעשה עמך] — but not לא תעמוד על דם רעך. And so we find with Nathan the prophet: ואני אבא אחריך ומלאתי את דבריך."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The bracketed text [בעמיך בעושה מעשה עמך] appears to be a gloss completing the midrashic reading of the verse; preserved as found in the source."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:20:02.828216547Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}